# Myriad (CR 702.116a): Wyrm's Crossing Patrol attacks Bot2 and Bot3, the other opponent, controls Liliana of the Veil (loyalty 3), so
# the token may attack Bot3 or "a planeswalker they control". Bot1 chooses Liliana: she goes to 2 and Bot3 keeps 20 life, Bot2
# takes 1. The token is exiled at end of combat. Declining (an empty `Target()`) makes no token: the loyalty stays 2 on the
# next attack (turn 7) and Bot2 takes only the Patrol's 1 again.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Wyrm's Crossing Patrol
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Liliana of the Veil
Swamp x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wyrm's Crossing Patrol.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot3.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot3.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot3.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot3.Hand.Liliana of the Veil.Cast
Bot3.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T4 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot3; Bot3.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil)
Bot1.Target(Bot3.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2; Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Liliana of the Veil
[T4 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot3.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Counters.Loyalty = 2
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot3.Life = 20
[T7 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot3; Bot3.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil)
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot3.Pass
? Combat.Attackers = Wyrm's Crossing Patrol > Bot2
[T7 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot3.Battlefield.Liliana of the Veil.Counters.Loyalty = 2
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot3.Life = 20
